            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PBPANCAKE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "OMGoodness! thank you thank you thank you!\nMy Aunt Sharon makes homemade pickeld beets and I cant get enough of them. When they are gone the store bought pickled beets dont even come close, but these do!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! I thank you from the bottom of my heart for this recipe. My son and I will eat these everyday!\nIf I could rate these 100 stars I would."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Teri Scott"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WOW!!!! My first attempt at making home made pickled beets....I pulled all the beets in my garden after the first freeze.....washed, cut about an inch above where the stems started then boiled whole for about 15 min. until I could pierce easily with a fork, cooled, then rubbed the skins off. Cut stem ends off and added the boiled vinegar, sugar and water and poured over the beets (mostly whole, some halved) and some hard boiled eggs, along with some salt and pepper and a few whole peppercorns. I also added a few cups of the beet water that I boiled the beets in. DELISH!!! I hope for great beet harvests every year and I will can these in pints with my pressure canner! (Minus the hard boiled eggs :)",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-16T23:35:31.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KimmieJo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe! I was inspired to try and recreate a Roasted Beet Salad from my favorite local pizza restaurant. I tried the Roasted Beet, Peach and Goat Cheese Salad here on All Recipes by Megancake using plain roasted beets and it just didn’t have that wow factor I was craving. I found this recipe for pickled beets and wow! Amazing! It was just what I was looking for! I used the already prepared beets from the refrigerator section at Trader Joe’s and it made this recipe so simple! If you haven’t tried these beets in a salad, I highly recommend you give them a try! I served them in a salad for a dinner party and got rave reviews!",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-30T16:19:09.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These beets are great and easy! I use fresh cooked beets and add about a tablespoon of dill to the brine one time. Another time I added cinnamon as suggested and onions. Very adaptable to different spices. An easy side dish for company. I also eliminated the salt as my husband is on a low sodium diet.",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-11T18:39:26.643Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristin Abbott Mokarry"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are so good! I used fresh beets that I peeled and sliced and also added sliced onion at the end. Just what I was looking for! I can't wait to make them again and again!",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-04T10:05:48.827Z"
          },
          {
